<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tiber River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tiber</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tiber is a river of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> that flows through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyrrhenian-sea">Tyrrhenian Sea</a>. Rome grew up at a crossing of the river, with access to the coast and to inland trade routes. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> note the city's origins on the Tiber as part of the foundation of Roman power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tiber-river.jpg" alt="Tiber River" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rabax63 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PonteSantAngeloRom.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
